        { "type": "note", "text": "Note: to play the chorus correctly and simulate the piano playing, keep the G on the" },
        { "type": "note", "text": "third fret of the" },
        { "type": "note", "text": "high e string fretted with your pinky. This makes the chords G major, Am7, Fadd9, and C" },
        { "type": "note", "text": " major. I also" },
        { "type": "note", "text": "suggest playing a Hendrix Fadd9, so wrap your thumb and play 1st fret low E string:" },
        { "type": "note", "text": "Am7   x-0-2-2-1-3" },
        { "type": "note", "text": "Fadd9 1-x-3-2-1-3" },
        { "type": "note", "text": "C     x-3-2-0-1-3" },
        { "type": "note", "text": "G     3-x-0-0-0-3" },
        { "type": "note", "text": "" },
        { "type": "note", "text": "The strum pattern for Intro/Verse/Transition is picked for the downs and strummed for" },
        { "type": "note", "text": "the ups." },
        { "type": "note", "text": "I suggest picking the A and D strings, and then up strum." }
